# Recorded deficiencies (append-only honest skip log)

## 2026-07-14 — W3C entailment corpus is self-authored, not upstream-vendored

The plan's "broaden the reasoner's W3C entailment coverage" set out to vendor the
upstream W3C OWL 2 profile suites and the classic RDFCore RDF/RDFS entailment suite
in place. The coverage spike proved this is not achievable by the inline-only
vendoring path: those suites express their entailment PREMISES and CONCLUSIONS as
reference documents (`mf:action`/`mf:result` IRIs, `test:inputDocument`/
`outputDocument`), not inline RDF/XML — so an in-place re-vendor grades ~0 entailment
cases AND a live re-fetch drifts the archive-pinned consistency corpus. Per the
plan's STOP-and-ask binary, the maintainer chose to author a small in-repo
both-inline entailment corpus (`entailment-mini`, like `tptp-mini`/`ontouml-mini`)
graded end-to-end by the `dl_entails` reduction. This delivers a real, drift-free,
non-vacuous coverage floor (4 graded cases + 2 honest structured-gap cases) but does
NOT grade the upstream suites themselves. Actually grading them needs a bounded
IRI-reference document resolver + fetching the full W3C test file tree and
reconciling live-vs-archive drift — a separate, upstream-availability-dependent
effort that is NOT done here.

## 2026-07-14 — `gmeow:gapShape` shipped as a matrix breakdown, not an OWL individual

The plan had two dogfooding items for the capability-gap boundary: (1) reify it as a
`gmeow:CapabilityGap` OWL individual carrying an enumerated `gmeow:gapShape` in
`graph/conformance`/`gmeow.gts`, and (2) ship a drift-gated `gmeow:gapShape`
breakdown consumer in `generated/agreement-matrix.md`. Item (2) — the binding
Finding-B "producer needs a consumer" requirement — is DELIVERED: the structured gap
shape is produced (divergence `profile.json`), carried (the tally carrier), and
rendered as the drift-gated "Capability gaps (by shape)" matrix section (byte-gated),
plus queried by `entailment_mini_gate`. Item (1) — the separate `gmeow:CapabilityGap`
OWL individual + `module.ttl` ontology terms — was NOT added: threading it through
the 26 `ExternalComparison` construction sites and adding SHACL-validated ontology
terms carried real determinism/regeneration risk against the remaining budget, and
the binding requirement is already met by the shipped matrix consumer. The gap-shape
data is therefore first-class structured data in the shipped matrix, but not yet an
OWL individual in the conformance graph.

