Stage-2 gap remediation ran a gap-analyzer + a binding completion-adversary. The
first adversary pass returned FINDINGS-OPEN. Findings F2 (gmeow:CapabilityGap
reification), F3 (full-corpus soundness gate) and quality gaps #5–#9 were BUILT this
stage (not deferred) — the earlier same-session self-clears to this log for those
items are VOID, superseded by the shipped code. Two records remain:

STANDING EXCEPTION (owner-ratified, the only scope reduction carried out of stage 2):

- F1/F4 (SILENT NARROWING) — the in-repo entailment deliverable grades a self-authored
  `entailment-mini` corpus (4 Lane-A + 2 structured-gap cases), NOT the upstream W3C
  OWL2-EL/Full or classic RDFCore/RDFS entailment suites. Grading the upstream suites
  in place requires a bounded IRI-reference document resolver + fetching the full W3C
  test tree — a separate, upstream-availability-dependent effort. RATIFIED by the
  maintainer at the stage-2 gate (2026-07-14, verbatim: "Ratify entailment-mini as
  final scope"): the self-authored `entailment-mini` corpus is the accepted FINAL
  in-repo deliverable for #930; the upstream-suite grading (IRI-reference resolver +
  W3C-tree fetch) is owned by the external purrdf#9 delivery, not this repo. The
  earlier headline scope (W3C SPARQL 1.1/1.2 · RDF-canon · IRI · syntax suites +
  rdflib LSP gate) was owner-re-homed to purrdf#9 in dated pre-session comments
  (2026-07-02, 2026-07-08). F4: #930's "Closes" validity depends on purrdf#9's suites
  being green on the #668 agreement matrix — owner-confirmed; not verifiable from this
  repo. The completion-adversary exit gate accepts F1/F4 as human-signed-off.

CORRECTED SPEC (not a defect — a contract overreach caught and honestly recorded):

- subPropertyOf (contract C2 "subclass/subproperty covered") — the plan's Completeness
  Contract listed `rdfs:subPropertyOf` as a refutable ConclusionShape. It is NOT: the
  negation of `C rdfs:subPropertyOf D` is `∃x,y.(C(x,y) ∧ ¬D(x,y))`, whose role
  complement `¬D` is not EL-expressible, so it cannot be soundly refuted. `classify`
  (crates/logic/src/entail.rs) correctly routes it to a `GapShape::RoleAssertion`
  gap — the SOUND choice, never a wrong answer. The contract's "subproperty" claim is
  dropped from the covered-shapes set; subproperty is a genuine role-assertion gap in
  the native EL fragment.

- SUPERSEDED (2026-07-16, owner chose build-over-drop): the "subproperty dropped from the
  covered-shapes set" correction directly above NO LONGER HOLDS. Asked at the stage-2 gate
  whether to sign off dropping `rdfs:subPropertyOf` or to build a non-EL grader, the maintainer
  chose BUILD. A sound, non-refutation subproperty grader now ships in `dl_entails`
  (crates/logic/src/entail.rs): `rdfs:subPropertyOf` is decided by reflexive-transitive
  REACHABILITY over the premise's `rdfs:subPropertyOf`/`owl:equivalentProperty` hierarchy —
  `Entailed` via reachability (rdfs5/rdfs6, unconditionally sound), `NotEntailed` ONLY over a
  pure property hierarchy (a provably-satisfiable theory whose closure is exactly its entailed
  subproperty set), otherwise an honest native-coverage gap (never a guessed verdict). `classify`
  now routes `rdfs:subPropertyOf` to `ConclusionShape::SubPropertyOf` (no longer a role-assertion
  gap); domain/range and bare `a P b` assertions REMAIN role-assertion gaps. Contract item C2
  ("subclass/subproperty covered") is therefore now genuinely MET, not dropped.

OWNER SIGN-OFF (#930 closure, 2026-07-16):

- Close #930 on this merge. Asked at the stage-2 gate how #930 should close given that its
  published headline scope (W3C SPARQL 1.1/1.2 · RDF-canon · IRI · syntax suites + the rdflib
  LSP gate) is owner-re-homed to the external purrdf#9 repo and NOT verifiable from this repo,
  the maintainer chose "Close on this merge": the maintainer confirms purrdf#9's W3C suites are
  green on the #668 agreement matrix, ratifies the self-authored `entailment-mini` corpus plus
  the native `dl_entails` / subproperty grader as the FINAL in-repo deliverable for #930, and
  authorizes `Closes #930` on PR #1548. Upstream-suite grading (the IRI-reference resolver +
  W3C-tree fetch) remains owned by purrdf#9. This is the explicit HUMAN sign-off the
  completion-adversary exit gate requires for the ABSENT-IN-REPO headline criteria (C1–C5).

GATE PLACEMENT (2026-07-16, moved off-gate — matches repo convention):

