  "Honest doc + drop inert fold"). The plan's original ask was to "execute both
  directions" (get∘put=id_view) for logic:Isomorphism. Investigation proved the
  reverse leg, seeded (as a recovery case must be) from the source, is
  MATHEMATICALLY ENTAILED by the section direction put∘get=id_source and cannot
  fail independently; and lower_recovery_case binds every view variable to the
  source, so the declared view is exactly im(get) — a section-passing iso is
  bijective on its declared corpus. A genuinely EXECUTED independent-view iso
  surjectivity check would require extending the recovery-case fragment with
  view-only witnesses; this was EXPLICITLY NOT UNDERTAKEN (out of #1383's
  Section/Retraction scope). LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md was corrected to state the
  reverse leg is "entailed rather than executed as a separate leg"; the inert
  two-direction fold was dropped so no hollow "both directions" code ships.

