## 2026-07-16 — #1572 removal of the live PurRDF entail cross-check (coverage reconciliation)

The live native-vs-PurRDF differential reasoning oracle (`gmeow-dev reason-crosscheck` /
`make reason-crosscheck`, driving `entail_crosscheck.rs` + `entail_oracle.rs`) is REMOVED with **no
live replacement**, by design. Under Principles 4 (single authority) and 7 (no downstream
duplication) the bundle-wide `native ⊇ purrdf-OWL-RL-subsumption` comparison was downstream
duplication of PurRDF's own compliance corpus, not an independent GMEOW specification, so it is
retired rather than re-homed. This block records the coverage reconciliation so the removal is
transparent, not a silent shrink (`.goals`: no silent capability degradation).

Reconciliation — every GMEOW-specific contract the oracle touched retains an engine-independent
witness (all offline, Docker/PurRDF-oracle-free):

- consistency / unsatisfiable-class detection → `crates/conformance/tests/dl_oracle_gold.rs`
  proves `native ⊇` the FROZEN external OWL-2-DL oracle verdicts over the curated OWL/gUFO datasets
  in `coverage/external/697-dl-oracle-gold/` (committed engine-independent gold), plus the native
  reasoner's own four-valued consistency verdict (`reason-verify`, on-gate).
- named subsumption / entailment preservation → `crates/logic/tests/ontology_entailments.rs`
  (GMEOW's own hand-authored entailment goldens, e.g. `proximity_measurement_is_a_measurement`).
- native coverage defects (the former `DlGap` class) → the native gap-zero DL·EL ledger
  (`meta:gate-dl-el-crosscheck`, `generated/logic/dl-el-crosscheck-report.ttl`, gapCount MUST be 0),
  computed from native results only (`full_parity.rs` certifies "no external oracle").

What is intentionally NOT replaced: the oracle ran its subsumption comparison over the **entire
folded EDB** on every gate; the retained frozen-gold exercises a curated dataset set, not the whole
bundle. That breadth was exactly the generic-PurRDF-compliance mirror the issue retires; GMEOW's
specific subsumption/entailment contracts remain witnessed by the named goldens above, and the new
`check_lane_purity` anti-reintroduction seal (this PR) prevents a live differential oracle from
silently regrowing. No GMEOW integration contract is left unwitnessed.

## 2026-07-16 — #1532 / slice authoring factory A2 (gmeow slice quality/lint consumer subcommands)
Adds `gmeow slice lint <dir>` (tier-domination gate + graded advisories) to the consumer
binary; `gmeow slice quality <dir>` already shipped under #1531 (commit da596648b, mis-trailered
`Closes: #1531`), so this PR delivers the genuine remainder: `slice lint`, the AGENTS.md razor
note, and the shared-engine subsume. The following are honest boundaries, recorded per the plan.

- ACCEPTANCE INTERPRETATION (user-confirmed 2026-07-16): the issue's acceptance clause "emit the
  same assessment the dev path produces" is satisfied as **faithful Bundle reproduction**, NOT as
  byte-identical dev(`ScoringEnv::Repo`)⇔consumer(`ScoringEnv::Bundle`) value-equality. Value-
  equality is impossible BY DESIGN: the two repo-anchored axes (doc-maturity, gmn1-coverage) read
  a repo-wide model under `ScoringEnv::Repo` vs a fresh single-slice model under
  `ScoringEnv::Bundle` (crates/slice-quality/src/score.rs:28-35, doc_maturity.rs:51-61) — an
  intentional A1/#1531 engine seam, not an A2 bug. The executable checks that DO hold: `slice lint`
  and `slice quality` derive from one `score_external_slice_bytes` SliceReport (advisory-code parity,
  tests/slice_lint_cli.rs test 8), and the existing `slice_quality_bundle.rs` ac5 test pins 12/15
  axes byte-equal across envs with the 3 env-dependent axes pinned exactly. No dev⇔consumer value-
  equality test was added because it would assert an impossibility; the divergence is the recorded
  boundary, not a chased bug.

- SARIF LOCATION (honest scope note): `gmeow slice lint --format sarif` emits warning/error-level
  results (severity grading works), and every result carries a `physicalLocation`, so GitHub code-
  scanning WILL ingest them — but the location is the engine's shared SYNTHETIC logical anchor
  (`ontology/gmeow.ttl`, `gmeow.syntheticPhysicalLocation: true`), NOT a per-finding location into
  the linted slice's own manifest.ttl/module.ttl. Slice-quality findings are slice-level logical
  diagnostics with no ingestion span (consistent with the source-adapter ingestion-spans model),
  so threading a real per-file location would be an engine change beyond A2's scope. The PR does not
  overclaim per-line code-scanning; the actionable value is the exit-code protocol + severity levels.

- TIER-LABEL LOCALIZATION (observed, pre-existing, out of scope): `--min-tier` resolves a tier by
  human label OR IRI local name (case-insensitive). In the embedded bundle the bottom two rungs
  resolve to FRENCH `rdfs:label`s (`Enregistré`, `Ancré`) while the top three are English — so
  `--min-tier registered`/`grounded` are rejected while `--min-tier tierRegistered`/`tierGrounded`
  (IRI local name) work. This is a pre-existing bundle label-localization quirk in the shared
  `resolve_min_tier` (unchanged by this PR; the dev `--min-tier` gate has the same behavior). The
  integration test uses the IRI local name (`tierRegistered`) to be robust. Not fixed here — it is
  a bundle/label-resolution concern, not slice-lint's.

- GENERATED ARTIFACTS: this PR touches zero pipeline inputs and its new finding code
  `slice-quality.lint.below-min-tier` does not project into any generated artifact; a full local
  `make sync` + `make check` were run and PASSED (all stages green). The branch's generated
  artifacts are left byte-identical to origin/main (a fresh sync surfaces only the pre-existing,
  #1570-tracked `logic:RecoveryCase` digest drift, which is unrelated to #1532 and deliberately not
  committed here to keep the PR scoped).

