## 2026-07-17 — Pydantic package cutover to purrdf::shapes::pydantic (flat single-module package)

User-approved capability regression: `stage-export-pydantic` was cut over from gmeow's
~2800-line hand-rolled slice-routed Pydantic renderer to
`purrdf::shapes::pydantic::emit_pydantic`. purrdf's emitter produces a FLAT single-module
package (`gmeow_models/{_base,models,__init__}.py` + `py.typed`), so the following
capabilities the prior renderer delivered are DROPPED, not re-homed:

- **Per-slice modules.** The prior renderer routed each class into its owning slice's own
  module (`gmeow_models/<slice>.py`, ~40 modules), so a slice's models were independently
  importable and a module's docstring carried the slice's tier/DOI header. purrdf emits every
  model into ONE flat `gmeow_models/models.py`.
- **Docs-digest linkage.** Every model's `json_schema_extra` used to carry `definitionDigest`
  (the term's `gmeow:definitionDigest`) and a rich class docstring (definition, when-to-use /
  avoid / how-to-use, worked examples, a runnable usage doctest, and a docs back-link URL).
  purrdf's emitter carries no docs-model integration, so these are gone; a model class now
  carries only its compiled-schema identity (no term-prose linkage).
- **Generated package `README.md`.** The prior renderer emitted a `gmeow_models/README.md`
  package-orientation file; `emit_pydantic` does not.

Wheel-version stamping is NOT dropped: `gmeow_models/__about__.py` (the ontology's
`owl:versionInfo`, PEP 440-validated) is still gmeow-orchestrated and stamped alongside
purrdf's artifacts, and `packages/python/pyproject.toml`'s `[tool.hatch.version]` still reads
it unchanged.

Forward path: https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/130 (upstream feature
request for per-slice module routing, per-class docs/definition-digest linkage in
`json_schema_extra`, and optional caller-supplied wheel/package version stamping).

The off-gate `packages/python/tests/test_conformance.py` (LIVE Pydantic conformance —
`make maint-pydantic-conformance`) asserted the OLD per-slice/docs-digest layout and was
DELETED as testing a layout that no longer exists (greenfield); the on-gate Rust structural
gate is unaffected.

## 2026-07-17 — LinkML/TypeScript/GraphQL developer schemas now cover exactly the SHACL shape union

The purrdf cutover moved the LinkML/TypeScript/GraphQL developer schemas from a hand-rolled
OWL→LinkML projection to purrdf's SHACL-derived `CompiledSchema` basis — the SAME basis JSON
Schema and Pydantic already used. Consequence: the developer schemas now cover exactly the
SHACL shape union. OWL-only / RBox properties that have no derived SHACL property shape are no
longer in these surfaces, even though the retired OWL→LinkML projection formerly included them.
Concretely, `gmeow:resentDate` and `gmeow:resentMessageId` (email slice, `gmeow:graphBoxRole
gmeow:boxRBox`, non-functional DatatypeProperties) are absent from
`generated/schemas/gmeow.linkml.yaml` and were already absent from
`generated/schemas/gmeow.schema.json` and `packages/python/gmeow_models/models.py` (the
pre-existing SHACL-derived surfaces), proving the SHACL basis never carried them — this is not
a projection bug, it is the intended unification. They remain in the canonical OWL/RDF layer;
their non-functional semantic is enforced there by the ontology-level structural assertion
(`slices/extensions/email/tests/structural.ttl`), not by the developer schema.

Forward path: https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/134 — purrdf owns the
schema-emitter output surface; the coverage narrowing (SHACL-shape-union basis drops OWL-only /
RBox properties) is an upstream limitation, filed as a request for the emitters to optionally
carry OWL/RDFS-declared-but-unshaped properties and to emit a coverage manifest. (A slice may
independently author an EL-safe declarative axiom in its `module.ttl` — from which the pipeline
derives a SHACL property shape — for any specific property it wants surfaced sooner.)

## 2026-07-17 — purrdf format-cutover: gmeow-side workarounds + declined cutovers, tracked upstream

The purrdf cutover exposed a set of purrdf output-format limitations. Per maintainer direction,
purrdf OWNS the import/export output formats: gmeow does NOT carry shadow re-implementations to
paper over them — each gap is filed upstream and gmeow either keeps a thin compensating adapter
(retired when purrdf lands the fix) or accepts the format's shipped shape. HUMAN sign-off (this
session): "Deficiencies NOT ours to own — file issues with purrdf; it owns the output formats.
Cut over, make issues and move on."

Thin compensating adapters gmeow still carries (delete when the upstream issue lands):
- LinkML slot NCName pre-pass (`crates/pipeline/src/stages/schemas.rs`
  `sanitize_linkml_property_names`) — exists only because `emit_linkml` hard-fails the whole
  document on the first non-NCName slot. Renames are reported as real loss, never silent.
  Forward path: https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/132
- SSSOM trailer splice (`crates/logic-compile/src/projections/sssom.rs` `splice_trailer`) —
  re-appends set-level `# #…` provenance that purrdf's `parse_tsv`/serialize drops, keeping the
  SSSOM output non-lossy. Forward path: https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/133

Accepted shipped-artifact scope changes (purrdf's format is what it is; no gmeow shadow):
- Developer schemas cover the SHACL shape union (OWL-only/RBox props dropped) — see the entry
  above. Forward path: https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/134
- JSON-LD serialization emits an empty `@context` (examples/goldens now use full IRIs).
  Forward path: https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/135
- `gmeow export` CSVW is purrdf's generic lossless RDF-1.2-in-CSV carrier (large), replacing the
  retired curated class/property/individual term-dictionary tables.
  Forward path: https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/136

Declined cutovers — surface kept as fully-functional native gmeow code because purrdf has no
equivalent generator yet (not degraded output; the native path is complete). Filed as upstream
generator requests so the native code has a retirement path:
- LPG scalability/selective-scoping (gmeow's statements-graph scope is UNCHANGED from the retired
  emitter — this is a purrdf scale gap, not a gmeow output regression):
  https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/137
- OKF export (ontology→OKF bundle generator vs purrdf's round-trip codec):
  https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/138
- Research objects (Croissant/RO-Crate/DataCite/Frictionless generators from RDF):
  https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/139
- DCAT (Turtle/CONSTRUCT) + VoID dataset-description generators:
  https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/issues/140

