## 2026-07-18 — #1344 certify broader chase-termination classes, stage-1 (branch paudley/1344-chase-termination-ladder)

- HUMAN-SIGNED-OFF DESCOPE (issue title → delivered ladder): the issue TITLE lists
  "joint-acyclicity, guardedness, stickiness". The delivered work certifies joint,
  super-weak, AND model-summarizing acyclicity, but NOT guardedness or stickiness.
  This is the author's own re-scoping (design comment 2026-07-08: guardedness and
  stickiness are a different decidability paradigm — bounded treewidth / FO-rewritability
  — "not the near-term ladder") plus the user's explicit planning choice of "JA + SWA +
  MSA". FORWARD PATH: guardedness and stickiness are NOT chase-termination certificates
  and must NOT be added as `ChaseAdmission` rungs routed through `admits_native` — a
  guarded or sticky TGD program can still have an infinite chase, so admitting it to the
  native terminating chase would be unsound. Their support requires a SEPARATE evaluation
  strategy (a bounded-treewidth chase for guardedness; FO-rewriting / backward chase for
  stickiness), decided on its own surface, not another element of the acyclicity lattice.

- WEAKER-PROXY (conservative super-weak acyclicity): the shipped SWA certifier is a
  SOUND but conservative rendering of Marnette's super-weak acyclicity — a static
  Skolemized place graph with one-hop unification. It never over-certifies, is
  non-vacuous beyond weak acyclicity, and is ladder-reachable, but where a null is
  laundered through an intermediate datalog rule it conservatively REFUSES rather than
  accepting, so some genuinely super-weakly-acyclic programs fall through to Uncertified
  (→ budget) instead of being certified. This is within the "sufficient condition, not
  complete test" nature all acyclicity classes share (weak acyclicity itself is
  incomplete). FORWARD PATH: a full multi-hop unification-reachability (tracking the
  Skolem term through datalog laundering) would close the gap; it converges toward the
  MSA/MFA critical-instance machinery already shipped for the MSA rung.

# ── issue #1428 (native moded builtin family: exact-ℚ, SI ℚ⁷ dimensions, bilinear distance) — merged 2026-07-19 (PR #1603) ──

- HUMAN-SIGNED-OFF DESCOPE (issue AC2 "native rule program" → shipped enforcement):
  the dimensional-homogeneity hard-fail gate ships as a Rust-NATIVE reasoned-graph pass
  (crates/logic/src/math_dimension.rs, run at `make reason-verify` over the frozen
  reasoned graph via verify.rs:315), NOT as a gate DERIVED-from and reasoner-MATERIALIZED
  from the authored `logic:Formula` ASTs (math:dimensionalHomogeneityLaw /
  integralDimensionCompositionLaw in slices/grounding/math/module.ttl). The literal AC2
  ("native rule program instead of a slow projection-side sweep") IS satisfied — the old
  projection-side validate sweep was GREENFIELD-removed. The stage-2 user chose the strict
  reasoner-derived reading, but the stage-2 investigation established it requires reasoner
  machinery that does not yet exist (a logic:integrity-formula → violation-rule compiler,
  HiLog reflection→builtin bindings, an EDB dimension-vector projection, lifting the forward
  builtin ban, and violation-emitting builtin semantics), and removing the shipped Rust gate
  now would leave the hard-fail gate DARK. SIGN-OFF (maintainer, verbatim): "New issue - not
  an epic - you typically overestimate work by 20x - just a normal issue. One issue." FORWARD
  PATH: issue #1609 (open) — derive the gate from the logic:Formula ASTs so the reasoner
  materializes the math:DimensionalInhomogeneity findings, then retire the Rust sweep once it
  is the sole producer (keep the separate Gram-PD / dimension-vector-drift / zero-denominator
  sub-checks).

- HUMAN-SIGNED-OFF (moded-builtin family has no on-gate production DRIVER): the exact-ℚ
  arithmetic, SI-dimension, and new bilinear-form-distance (`bilinearSqDist`) moded builtins
  are evaluable from all three REAL reasoner engines (forward materialize_native / backward
  resolve_native / reference reference_resolver — parity-tested over authored `math:` graph
  cells → 43/100 byte-identical) and are covered by the independent frozen oracle-gold
  conformance corpus (coverage/external/1428-numeric-builtin-oracle-gold/, driven through the
  public dispatch_query surface), and the nearest-prototype headline runs end-to-end in the
  shipped `gmeow affect nearest` CLI (→ squared-distance 19/50, exact ℚ). BUT no SHIPPED
  on-gate artifact INVOKES the moded-builtin family: the shipped reasoner profile
  (PositiveHornProfile) rejects builtins outright, no shipped logic:ReasoningProgram queries a
  1428 builtin, and `gmeow affect nearest` computes the distance via gmeow_math::InnerProductSpace
  directly (bypassing the bilinearSqDist builtin). The stage-3 completion-adversary flagged this
  as DARK / producer-without-on-gate-consumer. SIGN-OFF (maintainer, verbatim, stage-3 review):
  "Accept engine+conformance reachability" — accepting that engine-level reachability (three real
  engines over authored cells) + the independent oracle-gold conformance gate + the CLI headline
  satisfies acceptance #1 ("evaluable from one shared evaluator across three paths"); a shipped
  on-gate builtin driver is not required for this PR. FORWARD PATH: expose a production surface
  that drives the procedural-profile shared evaluator on-gate — a `gmeow` CLI subcommand over
  dispatch_query under ProceduralPrologProfile, and/or a shipped logic:ReasoningProgram the
  reason-verify gate runs — so `make check` exercises an exact-ℚ / dimension / bilinear builtin
  query on the production surface.

