## 2026-07-20 — advice-harvest advisory enrichment is native-only; the wasm validate surface keeps the raw Info finding

The advisory-harvest tier (a data-matching `logic:Constraint` at `logic:severity "Info"` →
suppressed `shacl.*` result re-projected as a `Severity::Note` `advice.*` finding carrying the
formalized term's `gmeow:howToUse` suggestion + `gmeow:useWhen` guidance + `logic:formalizes`
provenance + a `deonticRecommendation` `gmeow:ComplianceAssessment`) is delivered on every NATIVE
consumer surface: the `gmeow validate` CLI, the MCP `validate_local` tool, the repo validate path,
and the pipeline `stage-validate` (bundle self-validation). The advisory bridge
(`crates/validate/src/advisory.rs`) is `#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]`-gated because
`crates/validate/src/lib.rs` makes the `advisory` module native-only, and the crate's
`validate`/`validate_json` core must stay wasm-clean. Consequence: the wasm `validate_json` surface
still emits the matched anti-pattern as a raw `Severity::Info` `shacl.*` finding rather than the
enriched Note `advice.*` finding — a lossy projection of the advisory tier on that one surface.
This is a pre-existing native/wasm boundary, not a regression, and the issue's named deliverables
(the `gmeow.gts` bundle + the `gmeow` CLI) are native and deliver the full advice. FORWARD PATH:
make the advisory split wasm-compatible (or add a wasm-side enrichment pass) so `validate_json` in
the browser/wasm consumer also re-projects the Info match as the Note `advice.*` finding with its
suggestions/guidance.

