2026-07-22 — #1618 (purrdf parallel-SHACL bump): validate-gts REMOVED as redundant
================================================================================

- HEADLINE DELIVERED BY REMOVAL, NOT SPEEDUP (maintainer-ratified). #1618 asked to make
  `make validate-gts` "drop from ~50min to minutes" via purrdf's parallel SHACL. Investigation
  found `make validate-gts` (whole-bundle SHACL over the materialized bundle INCLUDING the
  multi-million-row reasoned closure — measured 2h+ on the merged bundle) is a strict DUPLICATE
  of the pipeline's `stage-validate` + `make validate` (authored-source SHACL against the same
  shape union, 0 violations in ~1.5-3 min) and `make reason-verify` (reasoned-closure soundness).
  The maintainer (2026-07-22) chose "remove validate-gts, keep purrdf 0.8.x": the `validate-gts`
  target and its CI `bundle-validate` job were removed; the purrdf 0.8.2 bump is retained (it
  speeds the on-gate `stage-validate`). No coverage lost — the norm-claims subset keeps its own
  focused SHACL test. This is a scope change from the issue's literal "make it fast" approach,
  ratified by the maintainer. The adopted "U1" enhancement (a gmeow:BenchmarkObservation census
  of the validate-gts wall-time) was correspondingly dropped: its subject no longer exists.

## 2026-07-21 — issue #1413 (native OWL 2 DL/Full fragment decision)

- The native DL-consistency reasoner now enforces hard existential-chase
  materialization backstops (a per-obligation witness ceiling of 512, a
  500,000-fact chase bound, and a 20,000-step backstop). A case whose
  existential / number-cardinality materialization would exceed a bound is folded
  into an honest `reason.dl-gap.chase-materialization-bound` incomplete gap (a
  WITHHOLD) instead of being materialized. This is a weaker-proxy mechanism than a
  complete cardinality decision procedure: large-cardinality cases (e.g. the W3C
  suite's `webont-i5-1-010` at owl:cardinality 127 and
  `webont-description-logic-905/906/907` up to 60000 — none among this issue's seven
  decided families) now WITHHOLD rather than DECIDE. It is sound — a withhold is
  never a wrong answer, so `corpus_only` stays 0 — and the bounds sit >2500× above
  the measured materialization footprint of every decided case (~8 chase steps /
  ~105 facts), so no in-scope decided case regresses. The prior behavior on these
  cases was an unbounded ~50GB heap allocation (a `>=n` cardinality lowered to n
  witnesses plus n*(n-1)/2 pairwise owl:differentFrom atoms; at n=60000 that is
  ~1.8 billion atoms), so the change trades an out-of-memory abort for an honest
  withhold. FORWARD PATH: a non-materializing / symbolic cardinality decision
  procedure that reasons over `>=n` and pairwise-distinctness constraints
  structurally (without generating n witnesses and n^2 differentFrom atoms), so the
  large-cardinality cases decide rather than withhold.

- The native RDF/XML ingestion path cannot grade 5 W3C `w3c-owl2-full` cases whose
  premises embed a `<!DOCTYPE ... <!ENTITY ...>>` DTD or an `rdf:datatype` node
  element (`consistent-but-all-unsat`, `webont-miscellaneous-001/002`,
  `webont-oneof-004`, `fs2rdf-literals-ar`): the hardened `purrdf` parser refuses
  DTDs (XXE mitigation) and rejects datatype-with-node-children. The external
  soundness grader now correctly treats these as pure SKIPs (a malformed/unparsable
  source is a corpus defect, not a reasoner capability gap) rather than spurious
  reasoner DlGaps, so `make maint-external-corpora` grades the remainder with
  corpus_only=0 and exits clean. This is a pre-existing ingestion limitation (the
  parser and grader ingestion path are byte-identical to origin/main and unrelated
  to this issue's seven-family reasoner work); the 5 cases are simply not graded.
  FORWARD PATH: route DTD-bearing premises through the existing `expand_xml_entities`
  helper (or a safe entity-expansion pass) before parsing, and support
  `rdf:datatype` node elements, so the 5 cases ingest and can be graded rather than
  skipped.

