## 2026-07-24 — #1609 (reasoner-derived math dimensional-homogeneity gate)

- MECHANISM TRADE-OFF (standalone forward chase, not the unified `reason_program`
  DL co-fixpoint — equivalent capability, not a capability loss): issue R1's literal
  step was to feed the compiled math `logic:Constraint` program into the closure
  `verify_with_reasoning_result` freezes via `reason_program`. The shipped gate
  (`crates/logic/src/reason/math_gate.rs`) instead runs its OWN literal-preserving
  forward semi-naive chase over a scratch world, because `crate::reason::build_edb_facts`
  is lossy for this purpose — it drops default-graph quads and, for `reason_program`,
  literal-object quads, and the ℚ⁷ dimension builtins need BOTH (verify's own inputs
  are default-graph Turtle and the exact-rational exponent cells are literal facts).
  Observable semantics are equivalent: after the stage-2 CRITICAL fix the gate's INPUT
  is the full reasoned closure (asserted EDB ∪ the DL-derived non-EDB edges), so a
  derived dimension triple is gated exactly like an asserted one, and the math
  homogeneity rules do not feed back into the DL strata so sequential-after-closure ==
  co-fixpoint for this rule set (verified by the stage-2 and stage-3 completion
  adversaries, which cleared it as a mechanism choice, not a deferral). The residual is
  a doctrine trade-off only: the reasoner now has TWO forward mechanisms (the DL
  co-fixpoint + this gate's standalone chase) rather than one committed path (§19).
  FORWARD PATH: make `build_edb_facts` full-fidelity (preserve default-graph and
  literal-object quads under an explicit profile) so the gate — and any future
  builtin-bound `logic:Constraint` gate — threads through the single `reason_program`
  path instead of a private chase.
